          "type": "SAssetFilter*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "String"
    },
    {
      "id": "does-asset-type-filter-exist",
      "name": "DoesAssetTypeFilterExist",
      "category": "SAssetFilterBar",
      "signature": "DoesAssetTypeFilterExist(Target, In Class Path)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "SAssetFilterBar*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Class Path",
          "type": "FTopLevelAssetPath&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "Check if there is a filter associated with the given class represented by FTopLevelAssetPath in the filter bar\n@param\tInClassPath\t\tThe Class the filter is associated with"
    },
    {
      "id": "set-asset-type-filter-check-state",
      "name": "SetAssetTypeFilterCheckState",
      "category": "SAssetFilterBar",
      "signature": "SetAssetTypeFilterCheckState(Target, In Class Path, In Check State, Enable Filter)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "SAssetFilterBar*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Class Path",
          "type": "FTopLevelAssetPath&"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Check State",
          "type": "ECheckBoxState"
        },
        {
          "name": "Enable Filter",
          "type": "Bool",
          "default": "true"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Set the check box state of the specified filter (in the filter drop down) and pin/unpin a filter widget on/from the filter bar. When a filter is pinned (was not already pinned), it is activated if requested and deactivated when unpinned.\n@param\tInClassPath\t\tThe Class the filter is associated with (must exist in the widget)\n@param\tInCheckState\tThe CheckState to apply to the flter\n@param\tbEnableFilter\tWhether the filter should be enabled when it is pinned"
    },
    {
      "id": "get-asset-type-filter-check-state",
      "name": "GetAssetTypeFilterCheckState",
      "category": "SAssetFilterBar",
      "signature": "GetAssetTypeFilterCheckState(Target, In Class Path)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "SAssetFilterBar*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Class Path",
          "type": "FTopLevelAssetPath&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "ECheckBoxState",
      "docs": "Returns the check box state of the specified filter (in the filter drop down). This tells whether the filter is pinned or not on the filter bar, but not if filter is active or not.\n@see\t\tIsFilterActive().\n@param\tInClassPath\t\tThe Class the filter is associated with\n@return The CheckState if a filter associated with the class name is in the filter bar, ECheckBoxState::Undetermined otherwise"
    },
    {
      "id": "is-asset-type-filter-active",
      "name": "IsAssetTypeFilterActive",
      "category": "SAssetFilterBar",
      "signature": "IsAssetTypeFilterActive(Target, In Class Path)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "SAssetFilterBar*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Class Path",
          "type": "FTopLevelAssetPath&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "Returns true if the specified filter is both checked (pinned on the filter bar) and active (contributing to filter the result).\n@param\tInClassPath\t\tThe Class the filter is associated with"
    },
    {
      "id": "toggle-asset-type-filter-enabled",
      "name": "ToggleAssetTypeFilterEnabled",
      "category": "SAssetFilterBar",
      "signature": "ToggleAssetTypeFilterEnabled(Target, In Class Path, Enable)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "SAssetFilterBar*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Class Path",
          "type": "FTopLevelAssetPath&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Enable",
          "type": "Bool"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "If a filter with the input class name is Checked (i.e visible in the bar), enable/disable it\n@see SetFilterCheckState to set the check state and GetFilterCheckState to check if it is checked\n@param\tInClassPath\t\tThe Class the filter is associated with\n@param\tbEnable\t\t\tWhether to enable or disable the filter"
    },
    {
      "id": "remove-all-filters",
      "name": "RemoveAllFilters",
      "category": "SAssetFilterBar",
      "signature": "RemoveAllFilters(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "SAssetFilterBar*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Remove all filters from the filter bar, while disabling any active ones"
    },
    {
      "id": "s-asset-filter-bar",
      "name": "SAssetFilterBar",
      "category": "SAssetFilterBar",
      "signature": "SAssetFilterBar<FilterType>()",
      "params": [],
      "returnType": "template<FilterType> SAssetFilterBar<FilterType>::~",
      "docs": "A copy of all AssetFilters in this->Filters for convenient access"
    }
  ]
